# Data conversion between mebibyte and tebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between mebibyte and tebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1MiB to 0.0000TiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MiB yields 0.0000TiB; backward, converting 1TiB to 1048576MiB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5TiB yields 1572864.0MiB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1MiB
print(forward_whole->to(TiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MiB
print(forward_fractional->to(TiB))
backward_whole: int = 1TiB
print(backward_whole->to(MiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TiB
print(backward_fractional->to(MiB))

<<< stdout
0.0000TiB
0.0000TiB
1048576MiB
1572864.0MiB

<<< stderr
